  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the mean deviation about the mean of the numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is odd, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "21",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that mean deviation about the mean of odd natural number is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>M.D&#160;</mtext><mfenced><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>x</mi></menclose></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>So, now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(given)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p>",
